=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  - Data sources (web useMaintenanceState/useUpdateMaintenance + useToast + useDateFormat
    + useId): bound through the P1/S8 seam ScheduledMaintenanceSource→ScheduledMaintenanceModel.
    The source carries the resolved MaintenanceState (mode / maintenance_message /
    maintenance_until) + query loading/error + mutation isMutating + the ticking `now`
    prop + connectivity; submitSchedule()/clear() mirror useUpdateMaintenance().mutateAsync
    ({mode,message,until}); MaintenanceActionOutcome drives the toast (web onSuccess/catch).
    NO HTTP in the view.
  - Composition (web GlassPanel + Badge + Input + Button + lucide icons):
      • GlassPanel `p-4 ring-1` + amber/blue/subtle ring -> TSGlassPanel + RoundedRectangle
                              ring overlay (within24h→statusWarning, active→statusInfo, else border).
      • CalendarClock icon (blue active / muted) -> TSIconBox(calendar.badge.clock, .info/.neutral).
      • Badge variant="info" "Maintenance active" -> TSBadge(tone:.info).
      • AlertTriangle "Within 24h" -> amber chip (exclamationmark.triangle.fill).
      • "Active until {formatDateTime(until)} ({n} min remaining)" / "Until {…}" ->
                              MaintenanceFormat.dateTime + MaintenanceCopy.activeUntil/until,
                              gated on minutesRemaining>0 exactly like web.
      • Clear Button(ghost, amber, X, "Clearing…") -> TSButton(.ghost)+xmark+statusWarning, disabled.
      • "Schedule a window" Button(ghost, CalendarClock) -> TSButton(.ghost)+calendar.badge.plus.
      • form: Input datetime-local -> DatePicker(.compact, date+hourAndMinute); Input number(min5,max1440)
                              -> Stepper 5…1440 step 5; Input message (maxLength 500) -> TSTextField (500-clamp);
                              Cancel/Schedule Buttons -> TSButton(.ghost/.primary), "Scheduling…" + disabled.
      • handleSchedule maths: dur=max(5, n||60); end=start+dur·60s; default msg
                              "Scheduled maintenance · ends {dt}" -> ScheduledMaintenanceForm + MaintenanceCopy.
  - States (ALL rendered, each with a #if DEBUG preview + projection/model unit test):
      loading (initial fetch → skeleton) · empty (resolved-but-unusable mode → ContentUnavailable) ·
      error (query failure → QueryError-peer + Retry) · active (message + countdown + within24h amber +
      Clear) · idle (hint + inline scheduler form) · stale (freshness chip + "data may be stale" banner +
      one-shot auto-refresh on transition) · offline (cached value + offline chip + banner).
  - i18n (P1/S10): web copy preserved verbatim ("Scheduled maintenance", "Maintenance active",
    "Within 24h", "Active until …", "Schedule a window", "Start (local)", "Duration (minutes)",
    "What's happening (optional)", "Cancel"/"Schedule"/"Scheduling…", "Clear maintenance"/"Clearing…",
    "Scheduled maintenance · ends …", and the five useToast messages); native chrome namespaced
